      "rationale": "As rendered, 'What is the capacity of the container in L?' supplies no container, no graduation and no reading, so there is nothing in the item from which a capacity could be measured. The competency's requirement to use appropriate measuring tools produces no graduated cylinder, measuring jug or any other instrument in any of the eight samples."
    },
    "comprehensive_coverage": {
      "verdict": "CONCERN",
      "rationale": "Litres and millilitres both occur as keys, so the unit pair is covered, but the tool clause of the competency generates nothing whatsoever and there is no item distinguishing when litres are the sensible unit and when millilitres are."
    },
    "cognitive_capacity": {
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "rationale": "Only whole-number readings are asked for, with no fractional graduations or part-filled containers, which would be the appropriate simplification for Grade 3 Quarter 2 had a reading actually been presented."
    },
    "variant_comprehensiveness": {
      "verdict": "FAIL",
      "rationale": "Eight samples share one stem that varies only between the two units. No pouring situation, no comparison of a container against a labelled litre bottle, and no alternate presentation of any kind is generated."
    },
